Quoting  archmage84  <archmage84@live.com>:
>1. I will be flexible with my build.

I think you're making a fundamental mistake by planning a "build",
MMO-style. The time to think about what you're going to ascend with is
when you're holding the Castle wand in your hot little hands (assuming,
yeah, you don't luck out and get an earlier wand). Even an early wish
should be focussed on immediate survival - with an eye to the endgame,
yes, but you've got to _get_ to the endgame.

Until then, the question isn't what you would like. It's what you can do
with what you've got.

> This includes swapping some
>artifacts, but when MR is so easy to get (either from a cloak or an
>artifact), I think SDSM's here to stay.

Well, reflectionless is for experts only (and even then, you'd have to
have a _reason_) so if you're intent on twoweaponing and the AoLS, there
isn't a lot of other choice. 

>2. Daggers have replaced Mjollnir, at least for the early-game.

It pains me to admit it, but throwing Mjollnir just isn't that good.

>6. I will be taking my time and clearing out every level. Always.

No, no, no. At some point in Gehennom this becomes pointless. Once Rodney
is dead it (even just trying to kill everything you see) becomes actively
counterproductive. On the Plane of Air it is rather like sending an
elegant embossed invitation to the Grim Reaper asking him to drop by.

>7. I can't really see me casting spells, can someone reassure me of
>this being possible with a Valk?

How high a success rate on identify do you need for it to be worthwhile?

Forget spellcasting in combat; but every class can use utility spells,
changing into as much spellcasting kit as possible.

>15. Holy water will breed like rabbits where I'm concerned.

Eventually you'll have a surplus.
